# StormChain Architecture Rules

## Component Structure

Every feature must live in its own component. `page.tsx` is routing only — no business logic, no inline UI.

```
src/
  app/page.tsx              ← routing + auth + global layout ONLY (~300 lines max)
  components/
    app/                    ← role shells and feature flows
      DriverShell.tsx       ← driver routing
      EmployerShell.tsx     ← employer routing
      DeveloperShell.tsx    ← developer routing
      DotApplicationFlow.tsx ← DOT feature (self-contained)
      ErrorBoundary.tsx
    ui/                     ← reusable primitives (Button, Card, etc.)
    [Feature].tsx           ← all feature components go here
```

### Rules

- **No inline feature rendering in shells.** If a page block exceeds ~30 lines, extract it to a component.
- **One concern per file.** A component renders one feature — not multiple unrelated sections.
- **Shells route; they don't build UI.** `DriverShell` switches on `currentPage` and returns the right component. It does not contain JSX for those features.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — feature logic inline in shell
if (currentPage === 'resume') {
  return (
    <div>
      <ResumeTabSelector ... />
      {resumeTab === 'upload' && <ResumeUploadWithVerification ... />}
      {resumeTab === 'create' && <ResumeBuilder ... />}
    </div>
  )
}

// ✅ GOOD — delegate to a dedicated component
if (currentPage === 'resume') {
  return <DriverResumeSection onBack={handleNavigateToHub} />
}
```

